  "notes": "M88 scenario (D-087, D-088, D-089; the layout agreed with the user 2026-11-12): incursion_objectives_44x60.json (the two New Recruit rosters, Incursion, on a 44\" wide by 60\" deep battlefield with 12\"-deep deployment zones on the short south (A) and north (B) edges, and M87's objective mission: Centre 1 VP, own home 4 VP, enemy home 8 VP from battle round 2, 1 kill VP per 25 points) plus 2D terrain, point-symmetric about the battlefield's centre (22\", 30\"). The three objective areas are terrain areas (14.01): the 12\" Centre holds a dense ruin, two L-shaped walls 5\" high and 0.5\" thick facing each other; each 6\" home holds an exposed 4\" crater (no solid feature in a deployment zone). A dense ruin (10\" x 6\", an L of 5\" walls open towards the near deployment zone) stands south-west and north-east, light barricades (8\" x 5\", two low walls each) south-east and north-west, and an exposed 3\" crater in a 5\" area on each long edge. Terrain is 2D (D-087): Exposed features block nothing; Light and Dense features are solid footprints no model may end a move on; only INFANTRY/BEASTS/SWARM/MOBILE models move through a Dense wall over 2\" (13.06). Areas holding Light or Dense features are obscuring (13.10), dense walls are solid (13.11), INFANTRY/BEASTS/SWARM models within an area have the benefit of cover (13.08, BS worsened by 1, D-089) and are hidden in an area with a dense feature unless they shot this turn or the last (13.09, 15\" detection range). Only the unit points and loadouts are taken from the rosters (docs/datasheets/, Games Workshop copyright, not copied here)."
